-- title:
--   Local equation uv=q^ew at a node of the resolved model
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $N_{0}\neq 0$ and a prime $q$ with $q\nmid N_{0}$, a Deligne–Rapoport model package $\mathfrak X$ of level $N_{0}q$ over $R_{q}$, a discrete valuation ring $O$ which is a domain, a ring homomorphism $\rho_{O}\colon R_{q}\to O$ such that the maximal ideal of $O$ is generated by the image of $q$, and an algebraically closed field $k$ of characteristic $q$ together with $\mathrm{to}\kappa\colon O\to k$. Let $\mathfrak X^{\mathrm{reg}}$ be a resolved model package for $\mathfrak X$ over $O$ with residue data $(k,\mathrm{to}\kappa)$, let $F_{c}$ assign to each $e$ and each $i\in\mathrm{Fin}(e+1)$ an ideal sheaf on the crossing resolution `Resolution` of $q\in O$ of length $e$, with $h_{F}$ asserting that on the $i$-th affine chart $F_{c}(e,k')$ cuts out the ideal generated by $V$ if $k'=i$, by $U$ if $k'=i+1$, and the unit ideal otherwise, let $\mathrm{ch}$ be a system of étale crossing charts for $\mathfrak X^{\mathrm{reg}}$ (read as a package with uniformiser $q$) labelled by $F_{c}$, and let $n$ be a node of $\mathfrak X^{\mathrm{reg}}$. Write $x_{n}$ for the image of $\mathfrak X^{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{nodeEquiv}\,n$ in the base-changed model $\mathrm{pullback}(\mathrm{toBase}\,N_{0}\,q,\ \mathrm{Spec}\,\rho_{O})$ under the first projection followed by $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{comp}\,k\,0$ and $\mathrm{bcMap}$, and $\eta$ for the generic point of `DRLevel.fibre0` (integral by the package). The assertion is the existence of specialisations $h_{\mathrm{Inf}}$, $h_{\mathrm{Zero}}$ of the images of $\eta$ under $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{comp}\,k\,0$, respectively $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{comp}\,k\,1$, followed by $\mathrm{bcMap}$, to $x_{n}$, and of elements $u,v,w_{0}$ of the stalk at $x_{n}$, with $w_{0}$ a unit, $uv=q^{\,\mathrm{width}(n)}w_{0}$, $(q,u,v)$ the maximal ideal, $(q,u)$ and $(q,v)$ the pullbacks of the maximal ideals at the two branch points along the specialisation maps for $h_{\mathrm{Inf}}$ and $h_{\mathrm{Zero}}$, and such that for every section $t\colon \mathrm{Spec}\,O\to \mathfrak X^{\mathrm{reg}}.Y$ of $\mathfrak X^{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{toBase}$ whose closed point maps to $x_{n}$, and every $d$ with $\mathrm{addVal}_{O}$ of the pullback of $v$ along $t$ equal to $d$, the closed point of $t$ lies in the support of $\mathfrak X^{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{comp}\,c$ exactly for $c=\mathrm{chainPos}(\mathrm{width},n,d)$, that is $c$ the first component for $d=0$, the $(d-1)$-st intermediate component of the chain at $n$ for $0<d<\mathrm{width}(n)$, and the second end component otherwise.
--
--   This is the local description of the resolved Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_{0}(N_{0}q)$ at a supersingular crossing: the stalk has an equation $uv=q^{e}w$ with $e$ the thickness of the node, the two branch primes are $(q,u)$ and $(q,v)$, and the valuation of $v$ along an $O$-section reads off which component of the chain of exceptional curves the section meets. It is used to extract node coordinates and to identify the thicknesses of the nodes in the level-$N_{0}q$ model.
